Z||000053||EdsB52||08-05-2001||07:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shiner:<BR><B>JohnnyK, thanks for backing me up.  <P>Yes, I WOULD say that to someone's face.  Nothing I say about people is a statement that I wouldn't make to their face.  That's how I am.  What can I say, sometimes honesty can be brutal.  <P>I would also like to bring up another point.  Would Grinthock get this mad if someone posted a STRAIGHT personal ad with his pic?  No, of course not.  If everybody here has nothing against gays, (I know most of you thrive on being PC), THAN WHAT DOES IT MATTER IF IT WAS A GAY AD!?!?!  <P>And one more thing.  "I thought the persecution of Christians was over a very long time ago... "  Songman, I have nothing against you, you seem like a real nice guy, but you must have never read ANY history book.  The Christian idea of god is resposible for millions upon millions of deaths, and persecution across the globe, through thousands of years.  <P>If everbody was insulted by my bible pages comparison, I don't care.  It wasn't meant as an insult to you people, and frankly, I can barely see how it was insulting to compare the thinness of bible pages to someones hide.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm not getting involved in whatever graphically occurred here, but I would like to say I agree with Shiner in the words of a respected columnist with the Arizona Republic; Freedom of religion should also mean freedom from religion.||||reg||1
