Z||000055||maryjane||08-05-2001||08:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>This thread is going off on a tangent.When it started,it had nothing to do with religion.It should stay that way. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You're right. Sorry, I'm through with it.||||reg||1
Z||000056||EdsB52||08-05-2001||08:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHeather:<BR><B>Amen maryjane!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>So there!<P>Yeah, and I would LOVE to re-butt some of those comments made on the MR2 board, but I dont feel like registering my nick...<P>Ive got 3.5 years of useful College and 0.5 years of University under my belt so far--I know a LOT of the arguements being pleaded there.  Most of the people posting on there are using arguements they may have heard on TV or casually on the radio/newpaper...  Sad, really.  People should start using their brains, not just going by what others have said/stated in passing.<P><FONT COLOR="red"><sub>*Heather deposits $0.02</sub></FONT></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Come on Heather, that's not a valid excuse for refusing to debate. It's excellent that you're pursuing college, what is your degree major? Are you major status yet? I know that's one of the hurdles I most liked to achieve, completing the required core so I could be major status. Then before you know it you'll be a senior, but the downside is that, at least at ASU you'll be a senior for a long time (ex: you're senior at 84 credits, don't graduate until 120). Anyway we all applaud what might be the greatest hurdle of your life. Now, back to the argument. If you're going to claim clout or you want your arguments to be qualified as more reliable because of formal education, you must engage in that argument successfully while reinforcing your opinions with facts and data. That's not coming from me, that's just the way it works. No one, except biased cheerleaders are going to be swayed by an argument comprised of, "I would argue it but I don't feel like speaking." Remember, if you want to win arguments, you don't argue with the people that already agree with you, you argue with those that dissent. You must construct your argument to refute and impeach theirs, not like Jsocha does with hysterical rhetoric.<P>"Most of the people posting on there are using arguements they may have heard on TV or casually on the radio/newpaper...  Sad, really.  People should start using their brains, not just going by what others have said/stated in passing."<P>Agree in part. Are you saying that the media is absent any valid arguments or facts? We shouldn't parrot the media, as I'm very critical of the media especially with their reporting of crime. But the media does convince a lot of people; they affect the outcome of many civil and criminal trials as the defendant is arrested, and before he or she has even had their initial appearance. I’m critical of that phenomenon and wish the media be restrained from that irresponsible behavior, but if they are then we as Americans are in the business of suppressing the media, which can be far worse than the former. The media is the focus of many college studies, I'm sure you'll find out. How can you be sure that most of the people posting are parroting what the media says/writes? Are you just assuming?<P>Now, my 2 cents on the Jesus or not Jesus arguments. I'm not going to post my position on this yet, so if anyone cares to guess which of the three major positions I assume and why, feel free. I've probably already given myself away, but don't be too quick to guess. Do you believe in the old earth or new earth theory? A devote Christian friend of mine enlightened me to the opposing theories where Christians believe the earth has been here 6,000 years and the scientific, possibly the Darwinian theory believes the earth has been here between 3.8 and 4.7 billion years. Most scientists agree dinosaurs walked the earth 65 million years ago. Do you see the predicament with someone believing in science and Christianity? That person must concede that one of their beliefs is inherently at least in part erroneous, at least in terms of chronology. So, since you believe in Christianity, do you also believe that dinosaurs actually existed? If so, how long ago? How old is the earth? See Heather, you need to formulate your arguments with your version of generally improvable facts (not that your facts are improvable, hence void, this is a subject based almost strictly on opinion) and exhibit them to the rest of the forum, or whomever your audience is and convince them that your version is correct or at least the most likely. Please do not take this as an attack. And please do respond, thanks, Ed.||||reg||1
Z||000057||JSocha||08-05-2001||09:26 PM||||I see Ed, that you are on yet another one of your...obvious...self, ego boosting, know-it-all, power trips in several threads again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||13
Z||000058||Songman||08-05-2001||09:47 PM||||Alright.. I'll keep it off religion....<P>Come say "Wah, wah, wah, cry me a frickin river!" to my face when I have been wronged. Just be ready for what happens next...<P>That is not a threat because threatening people is stupid.  Just a statement of how I am. To borrow from Will Smith, "Don't start none and there won't be none." <P>And you're right, I am a nice guy. But I don't say stuff to people who are obviously hurting just to make myself feel big either.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000059||EdsB52||08-05-2001||09:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>I see Ed, that you are on yet another one of your...obvious...self, ego boosting, know-it-all, power trips in several threads again.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Why you run smack in here and then email me privately is beyond me. You'll wine and cry foul but I think it's necessary to share this:<P>"Your so vane,<BR>You even thought that post was completely about you...<P>Dirt farmer?  Well, if that is what you want to call me, fine.<P>I am doing pretty damn good if I do say so myself if that is the case while<BR>others are folding, for a dirt farmer.<P>Respectfully yours,<BR>Jeff Socha"<P>I thought you were going to break into a Carly Simon number for a moment there.<P>I'm doing pretty damn good (well).....Ya, that's right, pretty darn tootin for a dirt farmer. I'm the liaison legalese guy for my business. Ya gots to get up way before da birds to gets one by me. They call me Marcia Clark around these parts, what exactly do they mean by that?<P>Sounds like you get satisfaction from watching your colleagues in your venue that have failing businesses. We're all proud.||||reg||1
Z||000060||FieroHeather||08-05-2001||10:23 PM||||Hey Ed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I do not take offence to anything you wrote in your above posting.  Actually I take delight in being challenged and stimulated intellectually.<P>Yes, the way that I worded my post above was a bit vague, but it was done intentionally.  I am lazy tonight, and I didn't feel like going beyond the "fluffy" response.<P>The reason I was stating my college/university training, was to give some kind of background to why I was saying what I was about to say --&gt; that most of the arguments made about dinosaurs/Jesus on the MR2 board were simpleton ones.  They were arguments that have been stated for years/decades in the media (print or visual or audio) and not very original arguments. <P>And NO, the media has a lot of power of persuasion over society, and I don't belittle them for it.  I was just stating that people have been getting their opinions from other people instead of thinking on their own about stuff that may really matter.  I spent like two to three years out of the media realm of things, and now, my first year back into it, I see how vile it has become.  With all of the swearing now on daytime/primetime television, no wonder society is going down.  But that is a DIFFERENT topic, Im trying to stay on the above mentioned topic...your post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I did not mean the implication of "most people on this *forum* parrot the media", but it was a broad statement/comment about society in general.<P> One thing I neglected to say was that I am a Bible Scholar, and Bible/Theology and Christian Education were my two majors in College (and Geography is my major in University, go figure!)  But just because I have a degree in something doesn't make me a "know-it-all".  It only makes me want to know more and also makes me realize how much <I>more</I> I need to learn.  I'll be in school for a total of 7 years, and I am only in year 4 so far...Im tired!!  But thankyou for recognizing that this may be the greatest hurdle of my life Ed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I know that I am supposed to "engage in arguments successfully while reinforcing [my] opinions with facts and data."  Of course, I know that.  Im just lazy tonight  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And I am NOT a cheerleader, nor would I ever want to be one (no offence to those who were/are).  I may be blonde, but Im a smart one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>As for religious theories and what I personally believe/know, I will take that into email if you'd like.  I am not out to shove what I know down people's throats.  If they want to know, they can ask me--Im not shy that way.  But this forum is about fellowship with people who love/hate Fieros (it is just that kind of relationship with them at times eh?) and to shoot the breeze about stuff that may be rattling around their brains.  This forum was not designed to make people "Christians" or "Buddhists" or "Atheists", but just "fiero enthusiasts".  So, lets all leave it at that, ok?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><FONT COLOR="red"><sub>*Heather deposits her $0.73 and calls it a night</FONT></sub><BR>||||reg||2
Z||000061||EdsB52||08-06-2001||01:23 AM||||What bothers me here is that someone who is obviously articulate is skirting an issue in which she participated and helped to perpetuate. <P>"They were arguments that have been stated for years/decades in the media (print or visual or audio) and not very original arguments."<P>Not original, yet not objectively resolved either.<P>"And NO, the media has a lot of power of persuasion over society, and I don't belittle them for it.'<P>I don't belittle them, but I am critical of them when they act irresponsibly. It's a First Amendment/suppression of the media issue, and I'm kind of on the fence with it. The part that pisses me off is how the media pampers guys like Jerry Colangello who is part owner of the Phoenix Suns and Diamondbacks. Colangello and has been obviously unscrupulous in the dealings of the teams in regard to tax dollars and stadium deals, not to mention running Barkley out of town. Anyway I don't think I've ever read anything derogatory about him in the local rags. The reason is obvious; he purchases a lot of advertising from them. Another adage is; don't make enemies with people that buy their ink in 55 gallon barrels. I would hate to live in a society where we have no media or the media is restricted. But I'm often not happy with what the media does or with whom they take sides.<P>"I spent like two to three years out of the media realm of things, and now, my first year back into it, I see how vile it has become.  With all of the swearing now on daytime/primetime television, no wonder society is going down."<P>What do you mean out of the media realm? Did you stop watching TV and reading newspapers? Actually, I think it was as vile then as it is now, but maybe I'm not the best judge of that since I love to watch the media and then hate what I see! I think it's unfair to transfer societies ill's onto the media. It's a gross rationalization to blame our children's problems and behavior on a box that receives a signal and presents a picture. This box does not invade itself into your house, or in the case of a radio or newspaper the same applies. You are required to procure these items from an external source, bring them into your house, apply electricity or open them up, and spend time absorbing their content. It's a very proactive and arduous task to initially get started into media involvement and to blame it for our kids shortcomings is, in my opinion another way of saying, 'we're bad parents, but it's not our fault.' Swearing, violence, and nudity are just semantics in my opinion. Are you going to pick up bad habits because you see someone else doing them? If so, would you be prone to start shooting heroine because you walked down the street and spied some guys shooting it? If you witnessed a bank robbery and found the robbers got away with $50,000 and were never caught, would you be prone to go rob a bank? If you witnessed a man beating his wife or a mother beating her children, would you be prone to do that? When I hear that I think of a morbid concept; legislating morality. Morality is purely subjective and since fewer than half of all Americans are practicing Christians, I would hate to see them or any group that is a minority become representative of the whole. Morality, or as I like to term it, ethics are within people and cannot be imparted into a person's persona. If someone practices or has the capacity to perform various unethical acts and television heightens the drama of the act, a person might act out on what they are already capable of, but I don't think people are programmed by the tube. Have you heard of or are you part of the contingency of people that thing metal music and some alternative music poisons the minds of children? I think the dynamic works in reverse order; people that are inclined to behave in destructive ways seek out mediums for ritual purpose like hard metal music and rave parties. These elements don't infuse themselves into the minds of people that are well adjusted, rule following people that have no inclination for that kind of behavior. Kind of like the Supreme Court's definition of entrapment; something that the defendant would have conducted or participated in without outside presentation. If someone is vulnerable enough to listen to a songs message and go kill people, then that person was a walking time bomb looking for an opportunity. I don't believe that the moral right actually believes that 'evil music' promotes violence. What the moral right really wants is to legislate what society listens to, dresses like, acts like, and every other facet of American behavior.<P>"One thing I neglected to say was that I am a Bible Scholar, and Bible/Theology and Christian Education were my two majors in College (and Geography is my major in University, go figure!)  But just because I have a degree in something doesn't make me a "know-it-all".  It only makes me want to know more and also makes me realize how much <I>more</I> I need to learn."<P>Sounds like a diverse education. And I agree; the more you know, the more you realize the less you know. You should, however, be able to formulate a cogent argument with what education you have and hope you will with me. Let's keep it public on the forum so we let others interact. Who knows, maybe you'll convince me of a couple things. And I wasn't calling you a cheerleader.<P>"As for religious theories and what I personally believe/know, I will take that into email if you'd like.  I am not out to shove what I know down people's throats.  If they want to know, they can ask me--Im not shy that way.  But this forum is about fellowship with people who love/hate Fieros (it is just that kind of relationship with them at times eh?) and to shoot the breeze about stuff that may be rattling around their brains.  This forum was not designed to make people "Christians" or "Buddhists" or "Atheists", but just "fiero enthusiasts".  So, lets all leave it at that, ok?"<P>I don't think you are trying to shove any theories down our throats. But as far as limiting the scope of topics in which we can enjoy, uh, this is the 'totally off topic' section.||||reg||1
Z||000062||artherd||08-06-2001||07:51 AM||||Just to take this nonsence full circle, I would like to point out that the "Fairy belived in by uneducated apes" was infact, at least technically correct.<P>So there.  That's what religion means, I personally belive we're all a contrived plot cooked up in a gelactic hollywood, and that we're currently being made into a movie that's gone over budget, striked on, bloated to nonsensicality, and had the 'script' desecrated to the point where it's no longer reconiseable.<P>There, now prove me wrong :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000063||grinthock||08-06-2001||10:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shiner:<BR><B>Wah, wah, wah, cry me a frickin river!  Contacting the police about something this trivial is pathetic.  Your skin is about as thin as the bible pages you guys are reading.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I was offline for awhile, so I didn't have a chance to respond to this as others did BUT....<P>First of all, like others mentioned had you said this to my face the day of the happeneing, it would have been bad, BanditBalz' girlfriend actually came over and told me to stay home, and not drive my car or go out because she saw how pissed I was.<P>AND HERE IS WHY.....<P>The day that happened a co-worker who is now a fellow fiero owner (and PFF reader, but not a poster) read it, he had mentioned it to my boss.  When I arrived at work I was pulled into the office and asked "what the hell is this", he may have said it as a joke, but when my boss starts seeing ****  like that, IT DOES have devistating effect.<P>As for the religious stuff guys, do'nt fight with FieroHeather, she has a BRE and other people have gotten into Theological conversations, bible argeuments and the like, and they always lose, infact, those that like to get into those conversations have given up on arguing with her......<P>||||reg||1
Z||000064||Ken Wittlief||08-06-2001||11:01 AM||||Someplace, somewhere, a preacher was talking about Jesus, and a person stood up and told his peers, "If what this man is saying is not true, then what he is doing doesnt matter - but if what he is saying is true, then nothing else matters".<P>everyone has to deal with the issue of religion and the reality of God at some point in their lives - and come to their own conclusions based on what is in their own heart.<P>"you gotta walk that lonesome highway... nobody here can walk it for you"<P>all the rest of us can do is tell you what we think, what we believe, what we have experienced<P>sooner or later you will realize the world is more than flesh and bones - supernatural things are real - things we dont understand at face value and cant explain with science<P>then you can either pretend you didnt see what you just saw, turn your back on it, or try to find a way to make it fit into your view of the universe<P>I was a skeptic when I was a teenager - I liked what Christianity said in concept, but I was not about to devote myself to something I could not prove was real. I was not gonna be a sucker for a bunch of made up stories.<P>  Over the years I experienced things, I learned things, I studied things, and by the time I was 30 I came to believe that Jesus is real, the Bible is an accurate message system written in 66 books by 40 authors over thousands of years, but yet its an integrated means of communication that has a single clear and important message. And its totally different from every other religious text ever written - almost the total opposite of every other religion on earth.<P>  But as to whether or not it can be proven - yes it can. Jesus said he would reveal Himself to people, that God would reveal Himself to people, now, today, while we are still alive.<P>  And all the skeptics and scientist in the world, all the dinorsaur bones or scientific theories cannot convince me that Jesus does not exist<P>  when He has revealed Himself to me<P>  just like He said He would.||||reg||10
Z||000065||JSocha||08-06-2001||11:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by EdsB52:<BR><B>Why you run smack in here and then email me privately is beyond me. You'll wine and cry foul but I think it's necessary to share this:<P>"Your so vane,<BR>You even thought that post was completely about you...<P>Dirt farmer?  Well, if that is what you want to call me, fine.<P>I am doing pretty damn good if I do say so myself if that is the case while<BR>others are folding, for a dirt farmer.<P>Respectfully yours,<BR>Jeff Socha"<P>I thought you were going to break into a Carly Simon number for a moment there.<P>I'm doing pretty damn good (well).....Ya, that's right, pretty darn tootin for a dirt farmer. I'm the liaison legalese guy for my business. Ya gots to get up way before da birds to gets one by me. They call me Marcia Clark around these parts, what exactly do they mean by that?<P>Sounds like you get satisfaction from watching your colleagues in your venue that have failing businesses. We're all proud.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ed, just continue like you are, parading around the forum and grandstanding with a "Look at Me, I'm smarter then you are attitude" by ripping peoples opinions or views apart like tissue paper and at the same time and in your indirect way, belittling/berating them through your inadvertent mockery because they do not live up to your level of intelligence.<P>I pointed out how obvious you are in another thread, when my intentions to begin with there was not to get into an argument with you, but to ask you to trim down your posts because they were becoming annoying.<P>However, apparently that was not good enough for you and you made a point to escalate a very simple request by jumping my sh*t, based on what I posted, to the point now where it has gotten out of hand.<P>I was just wondering how long it would take before you elected to post my email that I sent to you, that I was about to post on the respective thread.  However, prior to hitting the SUBMIT button, I elected to email it to you instead and see what you would do with it.  You did, exactly what I had anticipated you would do.  It was just a matter of timing for you to again, attempt to discredit me.  To quote you, "Your so simple and easy to manipulate" and you did exactly what I wanted and was anticipating you to do.<P>But, what are you really trying to accomplish "here" Ed?  Are you trying to berate and belittle everyone that crosses your path?  That you can start flame wars and arguments where none are needed or necessary?<P>Eventually, those that are unable to see through what you are doing at this time...like I and a "few" others have...will.  Sad to say, by that time the cancer that you are or have become will have either spread and have potentially destroyed members moral around here or forced members to leave at the fear of being criticized by Mr. Ed's over inflated ego of intelligence, should they post something that you seemingly find controversial or can twist to find ambiguity in it to make them either look foolish or like idiots.<P>Must make you feel like a real big man that you can come in here like an arrogant and pompas a@@ that you are and berate any individual that can not stand up to your ideals or what you have to apparently say for one reason or another.<P>Ask yourself, what is "your point" for doing this?  What are you really attempting to accomplish?<P>I really wonder if the persona you portray here, if you do this directly and randomly in public down in Arizona, i.e., challenging anyone?  Or are you just a coward in real life that has found a medium in which he can act bigger then he really is?<P>If you do portray this persona in real life and in public, I really feel sorry for you.  Someday, you are going to be without the safety net of the internet that you have come accustomed to and be a little over arrogant where somebody who you may cross isn't going to settle for what you have to say and might just put a cap in your belligerent a@@.<P>Do I wish this on you?  Absolutely not.  I wouldn't wish that on anyone, including my worst enemy (to which I have none).  Yet, if it does happen someday because you are so sure of yourself, all I can say is you brought it upon yourself.<P>At some point Ed, people <I>"will"</I> tire of it, as well as you and the negativity that you draw by always making an attempt to stir up the hornets nest each time just for the sole purpose of your self gratifying entertainment just to get an arguments going, just to demoralize them or piss people off  if they should be willing to take the next step to comment and attempt to come face to face with you and your apparent self destructive, condescending wrath.<P>It is apparent that you have absolutely no scruples or consideration for anyone else, other then your egotistical self.<P>Tear this post apart and twist it like you do or that of any others.  This is apparently all you know how to do, to once again draw negativity where it is not needed and again, stir up the hornet’s nest.<P>I won't argue directly and/or indirectly with you anymore after this post.  It just becomes an utter waste of bandwidth to do so.  And you can be rest assured, that should I make a comment in the future in any of my posts that you feel I am referring to you in one way or another, rest easy that I am not.  And if you do, then it is not I with a "fixation" problem, it is you and your over inflated ego.<P>I stand by everything I have said in the past threads, in an attempt to point out, if others have been following and where our recent argument originally started from and why, what may not have been obvious at the time to them, what you are apparently attempting to do here.  Driving a wedge into the forum and/or between members through controversy, arguments and or the belittling through demoralization of those that do not live up to your idealistic expectations.<P>Sooner or later, on the track that you are going down, it will also become obvious to them as well, as no one can maintain a facade for to long without themselves and their true intentions coming out.<P>If you give a man enough rope, eventually, they inadvertently hang themselves.  You're on the right track.  Eventually, people will tire of either your indirect attacks and your holier-then-now attitude posts, which seem to be a campaign to you of some sort.<P>People are not as blind as you think or apparently take them for.  It is that some of us have dealt enough with people  like you and are just able to see things a little faster because they are sensitized enough that it immediately stares them right in the face and they know enough to know what to look for to see through the charade.<P>Go ahead Ed, rip this post and any others that I may post in the future.  It will take a lot more then you to demoralize me.  And you will only confirm what I have been writing and pointing out all along.  And of course, it is of no consequence to me...a very proud "dirt farmer" from the plains of North Dakota.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000066||Songman||08-06-2001||04:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>And all the skeptics and scientist in the world, all the dinorsaur bones or scientific theories cannot convince me that Jesus does not exist<P>  when He has revealed Himself to me<P>  just like He said He would.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK Ken... Now I'm getting scared! We argee on something! HAHAHA<P>I never thought that the Bible was the Say All, Cure All for all men's problems, but it does represent in some way that there is a Higher Power and that we will be held accountable. <P>I have a lot of questions about the Bible, but I think that was the intent. I wonder how if Adam and Eve were the first people on Earth, how then the rivers running out of the garden went past cities. I wonder about the fact that science has proven that evolution exists. Not saying that we came from apes, but Man has evolved and that dinosaurs have been dated to millions of years before the first man. These questions I think are there to give us a desire to know more, and also to show Faith. The definition of Faith is the belief in something that you cannot prove.<P>I know that I feel better acting as a Christian. If there is no higher reward, no harm done. But if there is I am glad that I will be ready... And I don't feel like I have missed a thing.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
