Z||000068||Shiner||08-06-2001||05:13 PM||||Songman,<BR>   If would say that to your face if you got so upset at something as trivial as this.  I don't belive Grinthock got "wronged", as you put it.  If he had said that someone stole his car, or raped him, or something of the like, I would be the first one to offer him my consolations, honestly, no matter what kind of person he is.  That is not the issue here.  The issue is that he got WAY out of shape about a small issue.  If he gets this upset about this type of thing, imagine what he would do when something really wrong happens.<P>Heather,<BR>   I don't get television of ANY kind at my house, and I take everything I see in the main-stream media with a grain of salt.  I don't let other people decide what is right or wrong for me, and that is what this whole topic is about now.  I would also like to add that just because you have some higher education does NOT mean you are smarter than the rest of us.  I have seen complete dimwits come out after four years with a B.S..<P>  Belive it or not people, arguements like this are very enlightening.  Seeing other people's point of view is an important thing, wether you choose to dismiss it or not.||||reg||1
