Z||000086||Songman||08-07-2001||09:17 AM||||Ed, I have to give you credit. You are definitely the Master at taking a few words out of context and twisting it to try to make yourself look... to borrow something from our current religious topic... Holyer than thou.<P>And you wonder why nobody here likes you. Damn man, you disagree with everybody about everything! That is your right, of course... but at least use the words you choose to pick on in the context in which they were written.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000087||Oreif||08-07-2001||10:29 AM||||Just to throw out some thought's on this thread, If someone posts something as a joke, and it gets "out of hand" or the person starts posting it in other threads, to me that seems the joke was ment to be vendictive. It falls under the slander laws.<BR>The person who started the "AD" probably thought it was funny at first then as it started to get out of hand, decided to push it further out of anger to the responses. I generally don't care what others think of me. It's their opinion. But if someone started a "crusade" to post an AD like what happened and pushed it, (I never saw the posts that were deleted or saw the extent of how far it was pushed prior to being removed) I would consider that more of a personal attack rather than someone's warped sense of humor/opinion. I would most likely seek civil action as grinthock is doing and like he stated, it is being handled "privately".<P>As for EdsB52, I have read his posts before in other threads. Many of his long posts are usually non-Fiero related and have nothing to do with the topic. They are usually ment to start a debate or argument with someone. He enjoy's debating and seems to post messages to get folks to debate him. Now when I see his long winded posts, I just use the center wheel on my mouse to skip over them. ||||reg||1
Z||000088||FieroHeather||08-07-2001||11:27 AM||||Quote by JSocha:<BR><B>At some point Ed, people "will" tire of it, as well as you and the negativity that you draw by always making an attempt to stir up the hornets nest each time just for the sole purpose of your self gratifying entertainment just to get an arguments going, just to demoralize them or piss people off if they should be willing to take the next step to comment and attempt to come face to face with you and your apparent self destructive, condescending wrath.<P>It is apparent that you have absolutely no scruples or consideration for anyone else, other then your egotistical self.<P>Tear this post apart and twist it like you do or that of any others. This is apparently all you know how to do, to once again draw negativity where it is not needed and again, stir up the hornet’s nest.</B><P>Thankyou Jeff!!  I havent laughted this hard in over a week!!  I have one animal that comes to mind when I think of his personality type.  It begins with a "w" and ends with an "l"  LOL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Ed, thankyou for the lovely waste of time this morning...  You quoted me well, however, you took the substance of your arguments out of the things that WERE NOT THE POINT of my post.  I even STATED THAT they were not the point!!!  Way to go.<P>Everybody, get ready to bow to the almight Ed.  Oh wait, he doesnt have a chocolate bunny making factory, and he is not a pickle named Mr. Nezzer. (Inside joke for those who watch cartoons--which reminds me of what this has become).<P>Shiner: I did not watch ANY tv or barely go to the movies for two years, I did not read the newspaper, and the radio was always turned off cause I had my OWN music always on.  The *only* outside media was my classes, my conversations with friends, my textbooks, and the internet (which was for email, chatting and making web pages--not the news).  Pretty isolated, I know, but I was a TV/media junkie for over 10 years, with my tv watching time 35-45 hours a WEEK.  I stopped all of that, cold turkey.  Now that Im back into letting myself be exposed to the media's major sources of influence (TV, movies, radio), I can combat what they say with an open mind, and not take to heart everything they have to say. In a word, I can be objective.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Black88GT: you're alright in my view dude  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I apologize for ignoring your posts/comments since the crap that went on last month.  Thanks for the post.<P>Shaun41178: It was YOUR POST dude that brought the attention of the ad to the forum. You may have some explaining to do.<P>JSocha, Ken, Orief, and Songman, thankyou for your insightful posts.  As always, it is great to see people on this forum with a good head on their shoulders, and smart enough to use it properly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P><FONT COLOR="red"><sub>*Heather takes back her previous deposits, and goes and buys a drink of Milk.  No use in crying over the stuff previously spilt.</FONT></sub>||||reg||1
Z||000089||Ken Wittlief||08-07-2001||12:10 PM||||Personally I dont think believing in God is a matter of faith, or a matter of science.<P> Science is an attempt to understand the physical universe. Its based on observation of things that are repeatable, knowable, and that can be verified by experimentation. Science assumes the simplist explaination is usually the correct one, and science assumes that things have always been the same, or that they change gradually. Science cannot deal with discontinuties. If the amount of C14 absorbed by living things changed at some point, then all carbon dating is useless - same with mineral formation, same with the speed of light, same with time itself.<P>My belief in God is based on His communication with me. The Bible is a form of communication from God. It tells us who He is, what He is like, why we are here, and what is expected from us. If you take the time to understand it, to evaluate it openly and honestly, and you find written there something that you also find within yourself, an agreement if you will, then to me, that validates its authenticity.<P>  I found God, or maybe I should say, God found me, based on what is in my heart, not on what is in my head, and not because of some blind faith or some need to deal with my mortality.<P>  Faith is what I rely on to determine what to DO on a day to day basis. When I am confronted with a situation, with a decision to make, when I have to do one thing, or the other, sometimes opposites, then its my faith that lets me choose the thing that being a Christian has taught me to do, cause if I look with my eyes, if I reason with my logic, then doing the thing that Christainity would have me do is foolishness.<P> But I have faith that Gods way is the best way, so I do those things, which is an act of faith, and in the end, it always turns out to be the right choice.<BR> <BR> When I chicken out, and do what is right logically, when I only trust in what I can see, or what the rest of the world would do, then in the end it always turns out to be the wrong thing, and I end up regretting it.<P> Faith is like walking across a long bridge - you have to believe the engineers knew what they were doing, you have to believe the bridge just doesnt end suddenly with a 1000' drop with no warning, you have to believe the bridge leads to where you want to go, sometimes its pitch dark and you cant even see where you are walking. then its by faith that you take each step.<P>  Its not my intention to preach on the forum. I am simply sharing my experience, this is the way it has been for me, this is what works for me - take it or leave it at your own discression.<P>  Being a Christan isnt about what happens when you die, its about what happens today, how you feel about yourself, whether or not the creator of the Universe is a part of your daily life, and its about what you do day by day and hour by hour.<P>  Not because you have to. Not because you are told to. Not because you are afraid of what will happen when you die.<P>  Its because of what you feel in your heart. Its what you know is right. Its what will lead you to enjoy your life the most.<P>  And its because the creator of the universe Loves you like a son, and you love Him back like hes your Dad.||||reg||3
Z||000090||JSocha||08-07-2001||12:58 PM||||Althought baptized a Roman Catholic Christian and going to a Catholic school 5 out of 6 years (bad knees now...ahem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ), going to church every Friday at 11AM, praying every morning, afternoon and evening and sometimes going electively and later on forced to church Saturday/Sunday.<P>I eventually and personally formed my own view that the bible is just a collection of made up stories, legends or as a guide only, accumulated over time, much like the bedtime stories parents come up with to tell their children and that are handed down generation to generation.<P>I personally do not believe in a heaven or hell/God or Lucifer and that is just me and I do not force my personal view as I see it on others.  Because I do feel everyone has the right to believe in what they feel is right for them.<P>I personally believe we are what we personally make out of the life that i.e. creates our own Heaven or Hell, based on how we act in life or treat others.  If we work positivly in life, then we in est create our own Heaven and can rest peacefully.  If we are merely moving in life as a destructive force, then I feel when that time comes, we will rest in the misery we were so drawn to, or the Hell we create.<P>Its hard to explain my views, because, well they are my views.<P>If someone comes to me and explains their religion, I listen as I respect their choice and their views.  <P>If they come for the sole purpose, as it has happened in the past to save my sole and force their belief on me, I don't hate them for it as I respect them for having a strong dedication, but I do let them know, I don't force my personal belief on them or talk about it because of the contraversy it would stir, and ask them not to force their beliefs upon me.<P>I'm more for the theory we all gradually evolved due to the circumstance or to the scienific views without a grand creator and idol of life to idolize.  Sorry.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Please, do not be insulted by what I have said or think I disagree with your views.  Just sharing my thoughts and views on the topic at hand and respect you for all of yours.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000091||JohnnyK||08-07-2001||01:09 PM||||Actually I think Eds makes some fantastic points about religion (Science doesn't try to disprove relgion, in fact they would love to find existence of a god, however religion would call it blashphemy). Etc. In MY opinion (don't flame me for this), Religion IS just like fairy tales. They are stories with no proof at all (again, that "God works in mysterious ways" thing). Most of the time it has to do with the way you were raised. I always have this lingering guilt for not believing in God because I was raised to do so.Instead of searching for answers, people say it's a "big invisible man in the sky".  Whats the simpler, more possible explanation? That we were formed from gas and elements and took millions upon millions of years to evolve. Or some big invisible man took a rib out of some guy (who just happened to be beamed there by the way. It doesn't explain HOW he got there) and turned it into a women.||||reg||1
Z||000092||DRH||08-07-2001||01:50 PM||||I find it hard to believe the relative order of our existence came from pure random coincidence. It seems more likely that there was some guidance from an external source. I don't believe that external source takes the form of a literal translation of the God described in the bible. I do believe there is some base in fact for some of the stories it tells though.<P>What's so hard to believe about creating a woman from a man's rib? We may be able to do it ourselves within our lifetime. Cloning with a little manipulation to change the sex... <P>||||reg||1
Z||000093||JSocha||08-07-2001||01:58 PM||||Good points. <P>Just for a brief moment, imagine your the AIDS virus.  Overtime, via different combinations or strains it evolved into what it is today.<P>It may have been there prior in our make up (I don't know if we will ever know) or just because of a direct result through the culmination of the right circumstances and environments, BOOM...it in est announced itself as an organism and came to be recognized.<P>Just my quick take before I head back to work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000094||JohnnyK||08-07-2001||03:14 PM||||Whats so hard to believe about a rib turning into a women? The fact that there is no explanation. What happened, his rib flew out and grew into a women? I don't think so.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Anyways, unless you are obsessed and take the bible word for word (in which case you need some other sort of "professional" guidance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> , most Christians realize that Adam and Eve and fictional characters. A metaphor if you will.||||reg||1
Z||000095||DRH||08-07-2001||03:31 PM||||What I was hinting at is that maybe the supernatural powers attributed to God were the use of science as they would appear to people of the time.<P>A virgin giving birth? Piece of cake today.<P>Raining fire and brimstone on Soddam and Gomorah? The US did that to Hiroshima and Nagasaki almost 60 years ago.<P>Booming voices from above? Give me a helicopter with a really good PA system.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>A Zippo would appear supernatural to a caveman. It's all a matter of perspective.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000096||JSocha||08-07-2001||03:42 PM||||I just thought about that 80's movie with Val Kilmar in college and what they did to Bagley's (think that is his real name) head and the following scene:<P>"And ____________, quit playing with yourself."||||reg||1
Z||000097||Ken Wittlief||08-07-2001||04:14 PM||||Im not about to launch into a detailed explaination of Christianity or the bible, or of all the other religions I studied and explored in my personal search for the Truth. <P>If you think you can find inner peace by being a good person and doing good things then go ahead and give it your best shot. Let us know about 20 or 40 years from now how its going, or skip over the 'do it yourself' experience and read what King Solomon wrote concerning the human endevour of attempting to find fullfillment on your own - in the end he realized all his efforts were vanity and chasing after the wind.<P>  This is what I referred to about all the other religions - the rest think you can attain to a higher level through your own good efforts, with a little help from above, you can meditate or starve yourself, or be rightous, or do good things, or study and work hard, and in the end you will acsend to a higher state of being.<P>  Only Christianity teaches there is nothing you can do on your own to attain inner peace, there is nothing you can do to reach out to the creator of the universe, the harder you try, the harder you will fail.<P>  Somehow I doubt the Hebrew people wrote the old testiment for any reason, as a collection of made up stories - if you read it, all it does is point out how time after time God handed them the world on a silver platter, and they blew it, and He forgave them and let them start over, and they blew it again, over and over and over. This is not the kind of history people write about themselves, and its also the only religious text that so thoroughly condemms its own people.<P>  My only advice is to take your spirituality seriously, it is THE most important aspect of you life, no matter what you believe in - study everything - investigate everything - if you find something that 'suites you' 95%, then keep looking - your not there yet.<P>  and when you get to the point where something fits what is in your heart 100%, then you can stop looking, you have found what you are looking for.<P>  Just make sure you give Jesus and His teachings equal time in your search. Seek with an open and honest mind - listen to what your soul is telling you<P>  and remember, we are emotional beings, not logical beings - explain to me the logic behind love - you dont find God with your head, you find Him with your heart.||||reg||10
